=== (b) WITHIN-FIXED-SPAN MONOTONICITY (k=8, sets of {1..15}) ===
  Claim under test: within a fixed span, E(A)>E(B) => measS7(A)>=measS7(B).
    enumerated 6435 k=8 subsets of {1..15}, 8 distinct spans
    span=8: >=28 inversion(s); worst: E=320 set=(6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14) m=0.21617  <  E=(7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15) set=267/2156 m=304.00000  (gap 303.78383)
    span=9: >=150 inversion(s); worst: E=304 set=(3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12) m=0.13311  <  E=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10) set=419/1470 m=300.00000  (gap 299.86689)
    span=10: >=410 inversion(s); worst: E=284 set=(1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11) m=0.07262  <  E=(1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11) set=430/1617 m=280.00000  (gap 279.92738)
    span=11: >=796 inversion(s); worst: E=272 set=(2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 13) m=0.07234  <  E=(2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 13) set=8779/114660 m=268.00000  (gap 267.92766)
    span=12: >=1368 inversion(s); worst: E=272 set=(3, 5, 7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15) m=0.22590  <  E=(2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14) set=2318/8085 m=268.00000  (gap 267.77410)
    span=13: >=1840 inversion(s); worst: E=264 set=(2, 3, 6, 7, 10, 11, 14, 15) m=0.08905  <  E=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 14) set=73/245 m=260.00000  (gap 259.91095)
    span=14: >=1708 inversion(s); worst: E=344 set=(1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15) m=0.30882  <  E=(1, 4, 6, 7, 9, 10, 12, 15) set=109/490 m=264.00000  (gap 263.69118)
    => spans with >=1 inversion: 7/8; (envelope-counted) inversions: 6300
    => WORST inversion (span 8): higher-energy (6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14) (E=320) m=0.21617 < lower-energy 267/2156 (E=(7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15)) m=304.00000, gap 303.78383
  VERDICT (b): within-span monotone = REFUTED

=== (a) SINGLE-STEP COMPRESSION MONOTONICITY ===
  Claim under test: an add_energy-INCREASING single-element move never
  STRICTLY decreases measS7.
    examined 4000 sets; energy-increasing single moves: 12165; of those, measS7 STRICTLY DECREASED: 3201
